_name' ). str .replace_all( '_' , ' ' , literal = True ). str .replace_all( 'homer' , 'Homers' ). str .to_titlecase(). str .replace_all( r'Of ( \\d ) ' , r'Of $ 1 + ' )), y = 'stat_name' , x = 'pct_increase' , error_x = 'ratio_error' , labels = { 'pct_increase' : 'Percent Increase during Full Moon' , 'stat_name' : 'Home run distance' , }, title = 'Percent Increase of Homers during the Full Moon, 2024' , ) fig.update_xaxes(tickformat = '.1%' ) I guess 430+ homer rates look somewhat strong again? Yet, 440+ is essentially zero. This is definitely p-hacking, looking at a bunch of metrics trying to find anything that might look significant. I’m declaring Claim 3: Debunked . 7 Follow up, Home Runs, 2015-2026 Statcast data for computed distance is available since 2015. I had various issues getting the CSV downloads at Baseball Savant to work, something about the url was misconstructed. I copied out code from baseballr package to make my own CSV urls, and that worked. Show the code homersall_parquet = pl.read_parquet( 'statcast_homers_2015_to_2026.parquet' ) merged_all = homersall_parquet.join(moon_data, on = 'date' ).with_columns( * [ pl.col( 'hit_distance_sc' ).ge(d).alias( f\"homer_over_ { d } \" ) for d in range ( 380 , 500 , 10 ) ]).with_row_index( 'gid' ) homers_by_distance = pd.concat([ make_phase_bin_data(merged_all. filter (pl.col( 'date' ).dt.year().ge( 2015 )), phase_range = [ 99 ], range_size = 2 , max_full_moon = True , stat = stat)[[ 'ratio' , 'ratio_error' ]].assign(stat_name = stat, pct_increase = pd.col( 'ratio' ) - 1 ) for stat in [ 'homer_over_380' , 'homer_over_390' , 'homer_over_400' , 'homer_over_410' , 'homer_over_420' , 'homer_over_430' , 'homer_over_440' , 'homer_over_450' , 'homer_over_460' , 'homer_over_470' , ] ]) fig = px.bar( pl.from_pandas(homers_by_distance).with_columns( pl.col( 'stat_name' ). str .replace_all( '_' , ' ' , literal = True ). str .replace_all( 'homer' , 'Homers' ). str .to_titlecase(). str .replace_all( r'Of ( \\d ) ' , r'Of $